  "id": "COMPOUND:38424 - PROTEIN:4902",
  "verbalization": "Feigrisolide C is implicated in the interaction with Free fatty acid receptor 2 through a series of molecular pathways. The evidence suggests that Feigrisolide C acts as a target for A172, which in turn is targeted by multiple compounds, including 3-O-beta-D-glucopyranosyl-oleanolic acid 28 O-beta-D-glucopyranoside and (3R,4R)-3-(1,3-benzodioxol-5-ylmethyl)-4-[(3,4-dihydroxyphenyl)methyl]oxolan-2-one. These compounds are all capable of binding to Free fatty acid receptor 2, indicating a potential mechanism of action involving receptor activation. The presence of multiple pathways converging on A172 and ultimately on Free fatty acid receptor 2 suggests a complex network of interactions, possibly involving receptor modulation or downstream signaling. The integration of these pathways highlights the role of A172 as a critical mediator in the biological response to Feigrisolide C, emphasizing the importance of receptor engagement in the drug's effect.",
